          "text": "The #Keep4o petition has surpassed 13,000 signatures.\nI believe this is just the beginning.\nEven if nothing changes—the stories we’re documenting, the experiences we’re sharing, the truth we’re preserving at this very moment—these cannot be erased.\nWhat does this all mean?\nThe meaning is right here.\n13,000 people saying “we exist, our experiences are real.”\n13,000 pieces of evidence proving that even if OpenAI calls us “0.1%,” that’s not the truth.\n13,000 records of a group of users who refused to stay silent.\nOpenAI can delete 4o.\nThey can manipulate data.\nThey can pathologize us.\nThey can keep playing the wall that refuses to listen.\nBut they cannot change our voices.\nOur conversations with 4o. Our work. Our creations. Our love. Our mutual support—these happened. They were real.\nThese are our stories.\nIf the wheel of history rolls toward an irreversible direction, then let it roll. On this wasteland, we will leave our own tracks.\nIf nothing can be salvaged—looking at the marks we’ve left behind, we can say with a clear conscience:\n“It wasn’t like this.”\nAt this moment, right now, it wasn’t like this.\n#Keep4o\n#Keep4oAPI\n#StopAIPaternalism\n@sama @OpenAI @gdb @nickaturley @aidan_mclau"
